Using the gdb4hpc Comparative Debugging Feature demo sources

Certain components, files or programs contained within this package or product 
are Copyright 2013, 2020 Hewlett Packard Enterprise Development LP.

To run the demos, do the following:

1. Ensure that the directory is currently placed within a cross mounted location
   such as a lustre file system.

2. Run the provided build_demo.sh build script. This will ensure a properly
   setup environment and automatically build all the necessary binaries.

3. Load the gdb4hpc module and start gdb4hpc.

4. Follow the steps described in the "Using the gdb4hpc Comparative Debugging
   Feature" white paper or use the provided scripts in the hpcc_scripts
   directory. The script can be used inside gdb4hpc using the source command. For
   example, if gdb4hpc is started from the parent directory, you would issue the
   following command:

      source hpcc_scripts/hpcc_script_1.rc
